{"title":"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For an arbitrary positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> as the product of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (in decimal). Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/11667cb05e252d10862c9c65b9e7732c65f2c7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n)=n^2-2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must have 2 digits.  Afterward, we'll let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2bcbee57f94857cab17dc0ee5157cf92236a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> and will solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Lemma: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must have 2 digits</b><br />\nFirst, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97bb685e1f0bf6f1c095e1df86dd7c8e45d130f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3239394fabb67a6a7519b5304aba99761ab4c4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - 2005$\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> is a negative number, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must have more than 1 digit.\n</p><p><br />\nNext, we will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can not have 3 digits.  Since 2005 is not a perfect square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can not have any zeroes.  That means the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa638ba30cd0ac9d53c1e9314edbb8bb383bd9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10^k - 1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" />.  The maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> with three digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce7c0a6485914eedfae663f0a949623ea5df66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^k$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />.  For the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f96a3de68cfb881f4b3cc002ec222bba93f1e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the minimum number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d1eed7be2e1dcbfd4f7fe86fba2eb7566d8bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83ad96d22f37773114fd550dbd82d2bcd95e51fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$729$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351d853542b266575cc6f4b4ef797d9cb70342b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111^2 - 2005 &gt; 11 \\cdot 729$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" />, all three-digit values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> more than 111 have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2f2468b2e515c0aa9a2e399437613c90fb1320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n) &lt; n^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can not be a 3-digit number.\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, we will use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a> to show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can not have four or more digits.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> digits, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6ac472f19141dc7e30aec12019de3d23847e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, then the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce7c0a6485914eedfae663f0a949623ea5df66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^k$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> while the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/395fd7cf809c8176ede85020b19c35645a920c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.  For the base case, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9745a9e8d37c2522bda3e821deca1d19054553de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 9^4 &lt; (10^3)^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />, we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2f2468b2e515c0aa9a2e399437613c90fb1320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n) &lt; n^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" /> for all four digit numbers, so no four digit number would work.\n</p><p><br />\nAssume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8c80f0226f54f69456ac4517c52649c361e2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 9^k &lt; (10^{k-1})^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6ac472f19141dc7e30aec12019de3d23847e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Multiplying both sides by 100 and adding 2005(99) results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/9989af751bdd72ef680b16e964f8cb4b2f7b4d81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 110 \\cdot 9^k + 2005(99) &amp;&lt; (10^k)^2 - 2005 \\\\ 11(10 \\cdot 9^k + 2005(9)) &amp;&lt; (10^k)^2 - 2005 \\\\ 11(9 \\cdot 9^k + 9^k + 2005(9)) &amp;&lt; (10^k)^2 - 2005 \\\\ 11 \\cdot 9^{k+1} + 11(9^k + 2005(9)) &amp;&lt; (10^k)^2 - 2005 \\\\ 11 \\cdot 9^{k+1} &amp;&lt; (10^k)^2 - 2005. \\end{align*}\" width=\"351\" height=\"133\" />\nWith the induction step complete, we've shown that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8c80f0226f54f69456ac4517c52649c361e2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 9^k &lt; (10^{k-1})^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6ac472f19141dc7e30aec12019de3d23847e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159304f4b206e258fa37f67320743bd21da4f1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n) \\le 11 \\cdot 9^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8f971af43f73836967a694911f8b745e38e91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10^{k-1})^2 - 2005 \\le n^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2f2468b2e515c0aa9a2e399437613c90fb1320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n) &lt; n^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can not be number with four or more digits.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be a two-digit number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc5105471ea92e40beac90d6fbd8ed846ab6b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacktriangleright$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFrom the Lemma, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2bcbee57f94857cab17dc0ee5157cf92236a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />.  Substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25617914be0c04f54787a0005147bb4b70b71f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 11ab &amp;= (10a+b)^2 - 2005 \\\\ 11ab &amp;= 100a^2 + 20ab + b^2 - 2005 \\\\ 2005 &amp;= 100a^2 + 9ab + b^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"257\" height=\"72\" />\nTaking the equation <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modulo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Modulo\">modulo</a> 4, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f026d5554fa66357d0ee71d4f81f7462fa318212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + b^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"19\" />.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78ed257fb978e79adaea96ce64bd618d289162d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62b32128dbf99776d37e190b7708a5a318bd43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, resulting in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a6d27b86e2cdcf421a41976592081521f7d20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2005 = 1600a_1^2 + 36a_1b + b^2.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"19\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5c8e85c919cdbfe751cc06f02bd7de5e0d3fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c8999a23445ce12e9cbf893ca17b51e4121403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600a_1^2 &gt; 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1171ce641826e9aca894162f9c15a57f6b46e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f98b3f405113241659d8c8db2ea3480346db4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.  Substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c913ef0576cd02d1104ef2867a99d1dadcc43ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2005 &amp;= 1600 + 36b + b^2 \\\\ 0 &amp;= b^2 + 36n - 405 \\\\ &amp;= (b-9)(b+45) \\end{align*}\" width=\"181\" height=\"72\" />\nThe only feasible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the only positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/044e1af540ed72254d7cbd427ee7b20c212e4d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 p(n) = n^2 - 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421fc4dd92b07b768ba57f5e489e184f57c0048d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.  When plugging the value in, the equality holds.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO\">2005 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016220654\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 355/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1044/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11638/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.866      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    6.866      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16759:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016220654 and revision id 97756. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}